From 0dc70686048d73e7888c77319db116a997ea410d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: op-bench-framework <op-bench-framework@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:45:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 208/252] feat(op-bench): reusable single-operator benchmark
 framework (Q9)

Framework (python/pypto/op_bench) consuming the frozen U1 execution layer:
- OpCase object model validated against pypto.execution.op_registry (single
  OpDefinition source; unknown opcodes fail closed);
- provider registry with availability probe, version/sha256 fingerprint,
  timing semantics (pack/alloc/JIT/compile/dispatch), thread semantics and
  precision class for every provider (portable + AOCL LPGEMM bf16/f32);
- model/boundary/sweep shape suites (W8J 12-shape set embedded, sha256 cited);
- PERF_MEASUREMENT_PROTOCOL + ERR-0004 statistics (floor + UNSTABLE), warmup
  acceptance, UNGATED marking, no new thresholds;
- precision compare with derived accumulation band and separate
  semantic-difference / bug-triage verdicts;
- JSON schema validation, reproducible inputs (PCG64 seeds), raw samples,
  Q8 alignment block, Markdown + sha256sums artifacts;
- CLI wrappers and focused self-tests (schema, error injection, protocol
  parity with B3c, reproducibility).
